[{"id":2486745567,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6UOLnf","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Definitely easier to read. Maybe move it outside the global scope inside the class to call it like `Memory::get_offset` ?","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-2486745567","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-2486745567"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145"}},"submitted_at":"2024-12-08T07:13:50Z","commit_id":"25a0c9f5e750fe7c886c204dbe2b7f09cdb0b89e"},{"id":3267743513,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Cxc8Z","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Prerequisite to #105928, which was approved in yesterday's core meeting","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-3267743513","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-3267743513"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145"}},"submitted_at":"2025-09-25T13:39:33Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3268690419,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7C1EHz","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> I had it in the `Memory` as a static function first, it seems like static class functions cannot be truly `constexpr`. At least it refused to compile as such from my end, with a less than helpful error message\r\n\r\nAh! Glad I double-checked this. I ran into the same issue in #109744, and it came down to trying to assign `constexpr` variables with scoped logic before the class was fully declared. This can be worked around by initially declaring the variables as simply `const` within the class, then as `inline constexpr` outside the class:\r\n```diff\r\n core/os/memory.h         | 22 ++++++++++++++--------\r\n core/templates/cowdata.h |  4 ++--\r\n 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\r\n\r\ndiff --git a/core/os/memory.h b/core/os/memory.h\r\nindex 192394fdcd..441503803a 100644\r\n--- a/core/os/memory.h\r\n+++ b/core/os/memory.h\r\n@@ -36,11 +36,6 @@\r\n #include <new> // IWYU pragma: keep // `new` operators.\r\n #include <type_traits>\r\n \r\n-static constexpr size_t mem_aligned_address(size_t p_address, size_t p_alignment) {\r\n-\tconst size_t n_bytes_unaligned = p_address % p_alignment;\r\n-\treturn (n_bytes_unaligned == 0) ? p_address : (p_address + p_alignment - n_bytes_unaligned);\r\n-}\r\n-\r\n class Memory {\r\n #ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\n \tstatic SafeNumeric<uint64_t> mem_usage;\r\n@@ -55,9 +50,9 @@ public:\r\n \t//             └─────────────────┴──┴────────────────┴──┴───────────...\r\n \t// Offset:     ↑ SIZE_OFFSET        ↑ ELEMENT_OFFSET    ↑ DATA_OFFSET\r\n \r\n-\tstatic constexpr size_t SIZE_OFFSET = 0;\r\n-\tstatic constexpr size_t ELEMENT_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(SIZE_OFFSET + sizeof(uint64_t), alignof(uint64_t));\r\n-\tstatic constexpr size_t DATA_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(ELEMENT_OFFSET + sizeof(uint64_t), alignof(max_align_t));\r\n+\tstatic const size_t SIZE_OFFSET;\r\n+\tstatic const size_t ELEMENT_OFFSET;\r\n+\tstatic const size_t DATA_OFFSET;\r\n \r\n \tstatic void *alloc_static(size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align = false);\r\n \tstatic void *realloc_static(void *p_memory, size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align = false);\r\n@@ -90,8 +85,19 @@ public:\r\n \tstatic uint64_t get_mem_available();\r\n \tstatic uint64_t get_mem_usage();\r\n \tstatic uint64_t get_mem_max_usage();\r\n+\r\n+\tstatic constexpr size_t mem_aligned_address(size_t p_address, size_t p_alignment);\r\n };\r\n \r\n+constexpr size_t Memory::mem_aligned_address(size_t p_address, size_t p_alignment) {\r\n+\tconst size_t n_bytes_unaligned = p_address % p_alignment;\r\n+\treturn (n_bytes_unaligned == 0) ? p_address : (p_address + p_alignment - n_bytes_unaligned);\r\n+}\r\n+\r\n+inline constexpr size_t Memory::SIZE_OFFSET = 0;\r\n+inline constexpr size_t Memory::ELEMENT_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(Memory::SIZE_OFFSET + sizeof(uint64_t), alignof(uint64_t));\r\n+inline constexpr size_t Memory::DATA_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(ELEMENT_OFFSET + sizeof(uint64_t), alignof(max_align_t));\r\n+\r\n class DefaultAllocator {\r\n public:\r\n \t_FORCE_INLINE_ static void *alloc(size_t p_memory) { return Memory::alloc_static(p_memory, false); }\r\ndiff --git a/core/templates/cowdata.h b/core/templates/cowdata.h\r\nindex c04727cfa0..a772ecf415 100644\r\n--- a/core/templates/cowdata.h\r\n+++ b/core/templates/cowdata.h\r\n@@ -77,8 +77,8 @@ private:\r\n \t// Offset:     ↑ REF_COUNT_OFFSET      ↑ SIZE_OFFSET    ↑ DATA_OFFSET\r\n \r\n \tstatic constexpr size_t REF_COUNT_OFFSET = 0;\r\n-\tstatic constexpr size_t SIZE_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(REF_COUNT_OFFSET + sizeof(SafeNumeric<USize>), alignof(USize));\r\n-\tstatic constexpr size_t DATA_OFFSET = mem_aligned_address(SIZE_OFFSET + sizeof(USize), alignof(max_align_t));\r\n+\tstatic constexpr size_t SIZE_OFFSET = Memory::mem_aligned_address(REF_COUNT_OFFSET + sizeof(SafeNumeric<USize>), alignof(USize));\r\n+\tstatic constexpr size_t DATA_OFFSET = Memory::mem_aligned_address(SIZE_OFFSET + sizeof(USize), alignof(max_align_t));\r\n \r\n \tmutable T *_ptr = nullptr;\r\n \r\n```\r\nI'd also consider renaming it to `get_mem_offset` to match the naming scheme of the rest of the class, but I'm not gonna die on that hill","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-3268690419","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-3268690419"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100145"}},"submitted_at":"2025-09-25T16:55:19Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3269068377,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7C2gZZ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100145#pullrequestreview-3269068377","pull_request_url":"https: